WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.522
Quantization stores model weights with fewer bits.

00:00:03.522 --> 00:00:11.262
That can reduce memory dramatically and may improve inference efficiency, although there can be a quality tradeoff.

00:00:11.262 --> 00:00:17.097
Eight-bit and four-bit formats are common choices for local model deployment.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:25.072
The practical tradeoff is simple: use fewer bits to save memory, then evaluate whether the quality remains good enough

00:00:25.072 --> 00:00:26.440
for the task.
